---
/**
 * The flow mark: "X to Y" in a sequence.
 *
 * Replaces the literal → character, which does not render in this site's typeface. The
 * loaded Overpass subset covers U+2191 and U+2193 but not U+2192, and `unicode-range`
 * gates usage rather than mere availability — so every → fell through to Helvetica,
 * putting a second typeface on a site whose first typography rule forbids one.
 *
 * Drawn from the route stroke instead, the way the prose bullet and the tag separator
 * already are. A head is necessary, not decorative: a bare dash would read "Rp35M–Rp17M"
 * as a range rather than a sequence.
 *
 * Sized in em so it tracks the text it sits in — the same content-relative measure the
 * prose bullet uses for its optical offset.
 */
---
<span class="to"><span class="visually-hidden"> to </span><span class="mark" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>

<style>
  .to {
    display: inline-block;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .mark {
    display: inline-block;
    position: relative;
    width: 0.95em;
    height: var(--route-stroke);
    margin-inline: 0.3em 0.62em;
    background: currentColor;
    vertical-align: 0.22em;
  }

  /* the head, drawn — never a glyph */
  .mark::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline-end: 0;
    inset-block-start: 50%;
    width: 0;
    height: 0;
    border-inline-start: 0.34em solid currentColor;
    border-block: 0.27em solid transparent;
    transform: translate(0.34em, -50%);
  }
</style>
